+        <article class="profile-intro glass-card reveal">
+          <img class="project-mark" src="assets/championscode-icon.png" alt="ChampionsCode logo" width="82" height="82">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Authorized research</span>
+          <h1>ChampionsCode.</h1>
+          <p class="lead">ChampionsCode is a client-side Fabric mod for Minecraft 26.3 that brings an msfconsole-inspired workflow to authorized, defensive server and plugin research, alongside an explicitly enabled runtime Java addon development system.</p>
+          <div class="action-row">
+            <a class="button button-blue" href="https://github.com/International-Duck-Incorporated/ChampionsCode" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><svg><use href="#i-github"/></svg>View repository</a>
+          </div>
+        </article>
+        <aside class="profile-sidebar glass-card reveal">
+          <div>
+            <span class="eyebrow">Project facts</span>
+            <div class="fact-list">
+              <div class="fact"><small>Status</small><b>Alpha · 0.1.0-alpha.13</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>Technology</small><b>Java 25 · Fabric</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>Target</small><b>Minecraft 26.3</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>Fabric Loader</small><b>0.19.5+</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>Source</small><b>Public on GitHub</b></div>
+            </div>
+          </div>
+        </aside>
+      </section>
+
+      <section class="detail-grid">
+        <article class="detail-panel glass-card reveal">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Research console</span>
+          <h2>A terminal in game.</h2>
+          <ul>
+            <li>F8 opens a movable, resizable terminal with Console and Java tabs</li>
+            <li>clickgui and categorygui interfaces with typed option editors</li>
+            <li>Module registry with structured findings and explicit run controls</li>
+            <li>Command history, scrolling, colors, and confirmation redaction</li>
+          </ul>
+        </article>
+        <article class="detail-panel glass-card reveal">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Modules</span>
+          <h2>Passive-first tooling.</h2>
+          <ul>
+            <li>Server fingerprint, connection posture, and plugin-surface audits</li>
+            <li>Wire-lens and session-trace packet observation</li>
+            <li>Container integrity, transaction echo, and motion evidence</li>
+            <li>Chat plugin enumeration with silent and bounded aggressive modes</li>
+          </ul>
+        </article>
+        <article class="detail-panel glass-card reveal">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Safety model</span>
+          <h2>Authorization first.</h2>
+          <ul>
+            <li>Exact-host authorization allowlist validated on every run</li>
+            <li>One-run CONFIRM phrase and append-only JSONL audit log</li>
+            <li>Bounded, sequential probes with rate limits</li>
+            <li>No exploit delivery, credential collection, or stealth features</li>
+          </ul>
+        </article>
+        <article class="detail-panel glass-card reveal">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Development</span>
+          <h2>Current position.</h2>
+          <p>The alpha foundation builds, tests, and produces an installable Fabric JAR. Runtime Java addons compile real sources with a full JDK 25 behind developer mode and source-hash confirmation. No tagged release has been published yet.</p>
+        </article>
+      </section>
