+          </div>
+        </article>
+        <aside class="profile-sidebar glass-card reveal">
+          <div>
+            <span class="eyebrow">Project facts</span>
+            <div class="fact-list">
+              <div class="fact"><small>Status</small><b>Active development</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>Technology</small><b>Java 25 · Fabric</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>Target</small><b>Minecraft 26.2 / 26.3</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>Version</small><b>1.1.7.1</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>License</small><b>GPL-3.0</b></div>
+              <div class="fact"><small>Distribution</small><b>GitHub Releases only</b></div>
+            </div>
+          </div>
+        </aside>
+      </section>
+
+      <section class="detail-grid">
+        <article class="detail-panel glass-card reveal">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Protection surface</span>
+          <h2>What it defends.</h2>
+          <ul>
+            <li>Client brand spoofing with vanilla-like reporting</li>
+            <li>Network-channel, known-pack, and key-resolution filtering</li>
+            <li>Resource-pack cache isolation and local URL protection</li>
+            <li>Server-pack control with MANUAL, ASK, and ALWAYS ON modes</li>
+            <li>Chat signing, telemetry blocking, and account switching</li>
+          </ul>
+        </article>
+        <article class="detail-panel glass-card reveal">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Scope</span>
+          <h2>Honest boundaries.</h2>
+          <p>NullTrace does not make you anonymous. It does not hide your IP address, server-side activity, or every fingerprinting technique. It is specifically focused on reducing common client-side fingerprinting and tracking surfaces.</p>
+        </article>
+        <article class="detail-panel glass-card reveal">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Downloads</span>
+          <h2>Nightly builds.</h2>
+          <p>Automated nightly JARs are published for Minecraft 26.2 and 26.3 through GitHub Releases, the only official distribution channel. Any NullTrace JAR found elsewhere should be treated as unofficial.</p>
+        </article>
+        <article class="detail-panel glass-card reveal">
+          <span class="eyebrow">Diagnostics</span>
+          <h2>Stay informed.</h2>
+          <ul>
+            <li>Alerts, toast notifications, and detection logging</li>
+            <li>Optional /nulltrace debug command, disabled by default</li>
+            <li>Configuration through the multiplayer screen or Mod Menu</li>
+            <li>Whitelist modes for mods that talk to servers on purpose</li>
+          </ul>
+        </article>
